<title>JAPAN: Japan June cocoa bean imports up 7.9 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Japan June cocoa bean imports up 7.9 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-07-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's cocoa bean imports in June totalled 4,422 tonnes, up by 7.9 percent from the same month a year earlier, Finance Ministry data showed on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The following is a breakdown (in tonnes):</p>
<p>			June 97	  May 97	 June 96</p>
<p> Total		4,422	    5,073	  4,098</p>
<p>Major suppliers (in tonnes):</p>
<p> Ghana		3,525	    4,115	  2,788</p>
<p> Venezuela	    298		406	    236</p>
<p> Ecuador		365		331	    503</p>
<p> Brazil		 nil		120	    407</p>
<p>Cumulative cocoa bean imports in the first six months of calendar 1997 were 32,455 tonnes against 26,788 tonnes a year earlier.</p>
<p>Imports of other cocoa products were as follows (in tonnes):</p>
<p>			June 97	  May 97	June 96</p>
<p> Cocoa paste	   115	    190	   189</p>
<p> Cocoa butter	1,534	  1,230	   897</p>
<p> Cocoa powder	  623	    662	   998</p>
<p> Chocolate</p>
<p>  confectionery	578	    668	   742</p>
</text>
